1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,500
AI agents are everywhere. Building a good one still takes days.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:20,500
Every agent runs the same loop: reason, act, observe, decide.

3
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:32,500
Pick a proven technique, from a simple tool loop to a team of agents. Tune each move.

4
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:41,500
It works with any model: OpenAI, Gemini, Claude, Groq, or one on your own machine.

5
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:57,500
Learn it by doing: 48 quests in ten worlds, with red-team quests. Demos need no key.

6
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:11,500
Try it right on the page, with your own key. Watch every step, and attach files or images.

7
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:25,500
Debug any run: change one step and the agent runs again from there. Edit your team as a graph.

8
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:39,500
The Project builder plans, writes files, runs the tests and fixes failures. Illustrative run.

9
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:53,500
Test it: evals with a judge model, prompt-injection checks, and guardrails for personal data.

10
00:01:54,500 --> 00:02:07,500
You get real Python or TypeScript with limits, retries, OpenTelemetry and edge deploy files.

11
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:17,500
AgentSababa. Free, public domain, and it runs in your browser.
